-- title:
--   Multiplicative primes q≠ p persist for the rescaled Vélu quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and let $Q$ be a point of the Weierstrass curve obtained from $W$ by base change along $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$ and then to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, of additive order exactly $p$. Let $W'$ be a further Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ and $u$ a unit of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that the base change of $W'$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals the image of the Vélu quotient of $W_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ under the variable change $(u,0,0,0)$; here the Vélu quotient is taken with respect to the finite set `oddOrderSummingSet Q (p / 2)`, the set of coordinate pairs of the multiples $kQ$ for $1 \le k \le p/2$ (the point at infinity contributing $(0,0)$), and `veluQuotient` keeps $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and replaces $a_4$ by $a_4 - 5\sum_P t_P$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2\sum_P t_P - 7\sum_P w_P$. Assume moreover that $u^{12} = p^{k}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$. Then for every prime $q \neq p$ with $q \mid \Delta_W$ and $q \nmid c_4(W)$ one has $q \mid \Delta_{W'}$ and $q \nmid c_4(W')$.
--
--   The statement says that the integral model $W'$ of the quotient of $W$ by the subgroup generated by a point of order $p$, constructed via Vélu's formulae and rescaled by $u$, has multiplicative reduction at exactly the same primes $q \neq p$ at which $W$ does. It is used in the construction of the isogeny datum in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_quotientDatum_of_galois_stable_primeCard`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_quotientDatum_of_galois_stable_primeCard).
